{
 "$comment": [
  "MT (Masoretic) -> KJV-English verse map, for SWORD modules declaring Versification=MT.",
  "",
  "DERIVATION: libsword registers the MT system but ships no mappings_mt table, so",
  "translateVerse() would silently return its input unchanged. Canon shapes alone",
  "cannot produce the map either: a chapter-boundary SHIFT and a verse MERGE present",
  "as identical +/- deltas. This map was therefore derived from TEXT -- each MT verse",
  "was matched against two independent KJV-versified references (ASV and KJV) by",
  "content-word overlap, and per-chapter rules read off the consensus.",
  "",
  "VERIFICATION: all 23,213 MT verses map; every target lies inside the KJV canon;",
  "the map is monotonic within every book; and 12 documented Hebrew/English",
  "differences (Gen 32:1=31:55, Joel 3:1=2:28, Mal 3:19=4:1, Ps superscriptions, ...)",
  "are reproduced exactly.",
  "",
  "SEMANTICS: `off` is added to the source verse number; `dc` is the destination",
  "chapter. Any MT verse not covered here maps to itself. Several MT verses may map",
  "onto one KJV verse (88 of them: psalm superscriptions and genuine merges); the",
  "converter appends their text and records the original numbering in",
  "formatting.source_verses, so the merge stays reversible.",
  "",
  "",
  "CORRECTION (2026-09-15), found by tools/import/sword/verify/swordcheck.py on OSHB:",
  "- Psalms: MT and English share every psalm's chapter boundaries and differ only by",
  "  numbered superscriptions, so the Psalm rules are now DERIVED from the chapter-length",
  "  difference (MT minus KJV = 1: MT v2.. -> v1..; = 2: MT v2 -> v1, MT v3.. -> v1..).",
  "  The text-derived rules had missed the first body verse in several psalms (8, 77, ...),",
  "  mishandled the two-verse superscriptions (51, 52, 54, 60), stopped one verse short",
  "  (5, 9, 31, 48, 70; the converter then folded that verse onto the last one), and sent",
  "  MT 57:12 to KJV 57:5 because the refrain repeats.",
  "  Exception kept from the text-derived map: Ps 13 (equal lengths, because English splits MT 13:6).",
  "- Lev 5:20-26 and Num 17:16-28 now cover their last verse (5:26 -> 6:7, 17:28 -> 17:13).",
  "- Removed text-matching mistakes on short or formulaic verses: Exod 20:13-23 (+3; OSHB numbers",
  "  Exodus 20 exactly like KJV, so the rule shifted the Ten Commandments), Num 28:1 -> 27:6 and",
  "  Num 29:17-24 (-6). Lev 6:1 -> 6:8 (was 5:14) and Num 17:1 -> 16:36 (was 16:23). 1 Chr 6 and",
  "  Job 41 now cover their last verse (6:66 -> 6:81, 41:26 -> 41:34)."
 ],
